  "live_records": {
    "q-89652": {
      "dom_id": "step-q89652",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{{x}^{7}},\\, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0,\\, & x<1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<1 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$",
      "worked_solution": "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $x\\ge 1,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{x}\\frac{6}{{t}^{7}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={-\\frac{1}{{t}^{6}}|}_{1}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}+1 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
