    "q-89641": {
      "dom_id": "step-q89641",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{8{x}^{4}},\\, & x\\ge \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0,\\, & x<\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge \\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$",
      "worked_solution": "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $x\\ge \\frac{1}{2},$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {\\int }_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{x}\\frac{3}{8{t}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={-\\frac{1}{8{t}^{3}}|}_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8{x}^{3}}+1 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{8{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<\\frac{1}{2}, \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{8{x}^{3}}, & x\\ge \\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
