    "q-89631": {
      "dom_id": "step-q89631",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{2{e}^{x}}{\\pi (1+{e}^{2x})},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nfind the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{2{e}^{t}}{\\pi (1+{e}^{2t})}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡{e}^{t}}{\\pi }|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡{e}^{x}}{\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-89631-a",
