    "q-185532": {
      "dom_id": "step-q185532",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{21}x,\\, & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<2 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $2\\le x\\le 5,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<2 \\\\ {\\int }_{2}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 1, & x>5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{2}^{x}\\frac{2}{21}t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={\\frac{1}{21}{t}^{2}|}_{2}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{21}{x}^{2}-\\frac{4}{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-4}{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<2, \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}-4}{21},\\, & 2\\le x\\le 5, \\\\ 1,\\, & x>5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
