    "q-89700": {
      "dom_id": "step-q89700",
      "name": "Question 18",
      "problem": "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ 1-{e}^{1-x}, & x\\ge 1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(2<X\\le 4).$",
      "worked_solution": "We can perform this computation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<X\\le 4) & =P(X\\le 4)-P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =F(4)-F(2) \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-3}-(1-{e}^{-1}) \\\\  & ={e}^{-1}-{e}^{-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
